From f2a8af08eab413d7df1363012dda5cd3a404e6c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: three.js glass devices, black-hole/warp bridge, hero
 name fits

Hero
- the name is measured and scaled to fit its clip (--name-fit), at every zoom

Glass devices (three.js)
- sampler, cassette, player, knob and record modelled as single rounded solids
  with a clearcoated frosted shell, dark rim and opaque internals showing through
- one shared off-screen renderer and environment; each device copies its frame
  into its own canvas; drawn only when visible and posed
- scroll hooks pose them through a three-free registry; CSS solids remain as
  the fallback (no WebGL, failed import) and the tilt falls back to CSS
- used for the About's flying devices, the chapters and the bridge

Bridge v2
- keeps the sentence and the iris; adds a lit accretion rim
- devices spiral into the hole; the stack streams out as a word-and-ring
  tunnel; three frosted plates (real group text) settle out of the depth
- cables and docking removed; static composition unchanged in structure
